      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While I agree that for a couple of reasons adjustments to the friends system are needed, what you suggest is a bit over the top in my opinion. Why friend someone in the first place, if I deny him basic \"friend\" features afterwards? (I mean with that specifically the interaction ones like \"can join\")\nI would suggest instead, to be able to do some permission adjustments via grouping, like \"Friends can do XY\", \"Friends marked as favourite can do XYZ\".\nFor people with public exposure I would actually go away from the friend system and lean more towards to something like a \"follower\" system. (similar to insta etc.) An individual could then create a \"follower\" profile, where he/she can write different stuff into. People who would \"friend\" you due to current limitations to follow/join your events could \"follow\" you instead and for them to see if you are online or not, create one or two new online-status. Something like \"online+follower\" and \"join me+follower\" - as long as the \"+follower\" is not set, you appear offline for them.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
