      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2def4d22470972dc58f6a2|full_name}: Yes, my proposals may be a bit too much indeed. I mosly meant to open a space of discussion on this.\nSome reasons I can think about giving someone friendship but not join rights, would be to allow them to fully render my avatar when performing for instance, but not come to my private moments, where only selected homies would be allowed, without me having to rely on being orange or red.\nHaving a way to temporarily restict someone's hability to join me is important I think , too. \nI think the vrc groups feature could answer a lot of these needs , too.\nActually Secondlife has both groups and individual friends permissions, and in my experience, it prooved to be useful and effective.\nI think in their definitions, a \"friend\" is someone you allow to give you a set of permissions. I like this concept.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
