  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-09-21T09:57:25.806Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I find that as a social platform, VRC is lacking a finely grained friends permissions system. \nIt would be very useful to be able to set permissions individually for each friend such as :\n-Can see where I am, or not ( similar to color status, but set individually )\n-I can see where they are, or not\n-Can join me\n-Can voice me / I can voice them\n-Can see my avatar / I can see their avatar\n-Can interact with my bones or OSC  / I can interact with their bones or OSC\n-Can read my bio / I can read their bio\n-Can read my status / I can read their status\n-Can read my txt bubbles / I can read their txt bubbles\nThis could also be automated by using friends categories or groups, the friends settings being synced with the category settings.\nI can see a lot of situations where this would be really useful, including for people with public exposure such as DJs, musicians, avatar or worlds creators, events hosts, dancers, streamers, etc.\nRight now you can only friend someone or not, and use status to decide when people can join you or not, which leads people with huge friends list to always be orange or red,  preventing them to have a rich social experience outside of their creative activity.\nIt could be also very useful in a lot of everyday life situations. Someone can be a friend , but still not a super close friend, and as such you may only grant them a limited set of permissions. Or you may want to restrict them some permissions temporarily for privacy reasons.",
